Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 08:26:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1002/1002] SableOS: keyboard type-ahead on the Settings
 homepage

KEYBOARD_FIRST_SETTINGS_UX "Type-ahead focus navigation" at the top
level: with no text field focused, printable keys move the focus ring
to the matching homepage row (800 ms buffer, case- and accent-
insensitive, repeat cycles, wraps): S to Sound, SY to System. The /,
Search key or Ctrl+K open Settings search; Home/End/PageUp/PageDown move
by row. The keys work while the search bar or nothing is focused.

Reuses SableAppListKeyboard (Network access, App security) with a new
attachToWindow variant: it listens on the homepage window and adds
per-row extra words (sable_homepage_type_ahead_words, translatable)
that match only after titles, so "vol" reaches Sound and "lang"
System without taking a first letter from a title. Only keys no view
handled reach it, so the search field and IME keep their keys.
